---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { cadences } from "../lib/cadences";
---
<Base
  title="Cadence audio"
  description="Sources and public-domain status for the optional cadence recordings on Valor Record."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Sound</p>
    <h1>Cadence audio</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These tracks play only after you press Play cadences. Nothing starts by itself.
      The clips are quiet on purpose: the player opens at about one quarter volume.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each file is an excerpt of a recording produced by U.S. military public affairs and
      published on DVIDS with the public-domain mark. The records used here do not note
      copyrighted music. Commercial cadence albums are not used. Files are mono MP3 at 80 kbps.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The appearance of U.S. Department of War (DoW) visual information does not imply or
      constitute DoW endorsement.
    </p>
    <p>
      In general, Department of War visual information prepared by U.S. government employees
      as part of their official duties is not eligible for copyright protection in the United
      States. DVIDS also warns that some items can contain material owned by someone else even
      when they are not marked. These five records were checked for a copyrighted-music note
      before the audio was extracted.
    </p>

    <h2>Tracks</h2>
    {
      cadences.map((track) => (
        <article class="cadence-credit">
          <h3>
            {track.title}
            <span class="badge">{track.branch}</span>
          </h3>
          <p>{track.caller}</p>
          <p class="meta">
            {track.unit}. {track.place}. Recorded {track.recorded}. {track.credit}. VIRIN {track.virin}.
          </p>
          <p>{track.clip}</p>
          <p>{track.license}</p>
          <p>
            <a href={track.sourceUrl}>DVIDS source recording</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      ))
    }

    <h2>Branches not included</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Navy. A Great Lakes cadence-off from March 2025 is on DVIDS as still photographs, not as
        a recording of sailors calling cadence. No public-domain or Creative Commons Navy cadence
        audio was found.
      </li>
      <li>
        Air Force. No government cadence recording was found that was both a clean cadence call
        and free of a noted music bed.
      </li>
      <li>
        Coast Guard. No public-domain cadence recording was found.
      </li>
      <li>
        A separate Airborne or Ranger unit recording was not found. The Airborne Ranger track above
        is the cadence as called by an Army field-artillery drill sergeant at Fort Sill.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
